2026-02-10 22:36:31,733 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document What Happens If Investors Hold a Futures Contract Until Expiration?

When equities are the underlying asset, traders who hold futures contracts until expiration settle their positions in cash. The trader will pay or receive a cash settlement depending on whether the underlying asset increased or decreased during the investment holding period. In some cases, however, futures contracts require physical delivery. In this scenario, the investor holding the contract until expiration would take delivery of the underlying asset. is relevant
