The credit spread is the result of the difference in risk. Corporate bonds come with more risk than U.S. Treasury bonds, so they need to offer higher yields to attract investors. The price you pay for either bond may be the same, but you are assuming a higher risk with corporate bonds, which means you need to be compensated with higher earnings potential. is NOT relevant, dump it.
